 "text": "Hello there! How's your day treating you? Keep a safe distance, usually at least twice the length of the car in front of you. That way, if they stop quickly, you have time to slow down Sorry to sound harsh, but they should have thought of that before parked so close. If they do get annoyed, it's their problem, not yours. Come to a complete stop, check both ways, and only proceed when it' safe. Rough riding isn't worth any time savings. It is, and it only happens because people park too close. If everyone pulled over just one car length further, it'd be much safer for everyone.",
